 bool←txt KeepOneDoubleMarkerPerRun bool;starts;ends;opener
⍝ `bool` is the result of something like `'**'⍷txt`, which finds overlapping hits in a run of
⍝ three or more markers: `'**'⍷'***'` is `1 1 0`. Keeps a single hit per run: the first one when
⍝ the run opens (a non-white-space character follows it), otherwise the last one.
⍝ That way "***x***" ends up as "<strong>*x*</strong>", and the remaining single markers are
⍝ processed as <em> later on.
⍝ `txt` must be padded with at least two blanks at both ends.
 starts←⍸bool∧~0,¯1↓bool
 ends←⍸bool∧~1↓bool,0
 opener←~txt[ends+2]∊AllWhiteSpaceChars
 bool←(≢bool)⍴0
 bool[(opener×starts)+(~opener)×ends]←1
